# With two opponents Valki's trigger has both reveal their hands and Bot1 exile one creature card from each (the Grizzly Bears
# and the Balduvian Bears, both mana value 2), the Islands left (CR 608.2c, "for each opponent"). {X} with X=2 then
# chooses one creature card of the two, not both, and Valki becomes a copy of that one (CR 707.2).

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Valki, God of Lies
Island x22

[Bot2 Deck]
Grizzly Bears
Island x22

[Bot3 Deck]
Balduvian Bears
Island x22

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Valki, God of Lies.Cast
Bot1.Choose(Grizzly Bears)
Bot1.Choose(Balduvian Bears)
? Exile = Balduvian Bears; Grizzly Bears
? Bot2.Hand.Count = 6
? Bot3.Hand.Count = 6
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Valki, God of Lies.Activate(X: 2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Choose(Balduvian Bears)
? Bot1.Battlefield.Balduvian Bears.Toughness = 2
[T1 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Balduvian Bears.Power = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Valki, God of Lies = (absent)
Exile = Balduvian Bears; Grizzly Bears
